  "result": "News | Ryosuke Takata (https://bonochof.github.io/news/)\nciteturn7284view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://bonochof.github.io/news/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 119\nL0: [Input]\nL1: \nL2: cite0†Home cite1†About cite2†Works cite3†News cite4†日本語 L3: \nL4: Ryosuke Takata\nL5: \nL6: cite5†Image L7: \nL8: Project Researcher at the University of Tokyo\nL9: \nL10: # News\nL11: ## 2026 (9)\nL12:   * 2026.09.08 Poster presentation at HUMAI Summer Session 2026. The title is \"Emergence of Organized Collective Behavior from Kick the Can Game.\" And received the Poster Presentation Award.\nL13:   * 2026.06.30 Co-authored preprint published. The title is \"OpenLife: Toward Open-World Artificial Life with Autonomous LLM Agents.\" cite6†arXiv:2606.31046†arxiv.org L14:   * 2026.06.17 Paper accepted at Collective Intelligence Journal. The title is \"Evolution of Collective Behavior from Individually Optimized Chemotactic Agents.\"\nL15:   * 2026.05.19 Paper accepted at Artificial Life Journal. The title is \"Communication, Embodiment, and Coordination in an El Farol Bar-Inspired LLM Society.\"\nL16:   * 2026.05.12 Accepted for a research grant from The Nippon Foundation HUMAI Program. The research theme is \"Emergence Mechanisms of Irrational Play Interactions in AI Agents.\"\nL17:   * 2026.04.06 Co-authored paper accepted at ACL2026. The title is \"From Heard to Lived Opinions: Simulating Opinion Dynamics with Grounded LLM Agents in Economic Environments.\"\nL18:   * 2026.03.10 Oral presentation at the Ikegami Lab Symposium. The title is \"Agent Language Space Project.\"\nL19:   * 2026.03.09 Accepted for a research grant from the Support Center for Advanced Telecommunications Technology Research (SCAT). The research theme is \"Constructive Dialogue Support System Using Discourse Space Maps and Intellectually Curious Agents.\"\nL20:   * 2026.02.27 Accepted for a research grant from the Grant-in-Aid for Young Scientists. The research theme is \"Multi-Agent Language Emergence Based on Functional Requirements and Elucidation of Structuring Principles.\"\nL21: ## 2025 (9)\nL22:   * 2025.12.18 Oral presentation at the Complex Systems Conference. The title is \"LLM Multi-Agent Simulation: Emerging Individuality and Strategies from Collective Interaction.\"\nL23:   * 2025.11.07 Co-authored preprint published. The title is \"Emergence from Emergence: Financial Market Simulation via Learning with Heterogeneous Preferences.\" cite7†arXiv:2511.05207†arxiv.org L24:   * 2025.10.07 Poster presentation at ALIFE2025. The title is \"Internalized Culture versus External Rules: The Emergence of Bounded Rationality in LLM Agent Societies.\"\nL25:   * 2025.09.04 Preprint published. The title is \"Emergent Social Dynamics of LLM Agents in the El Farol Bar Problem.\" cite8†arXiv:2509.04537†arxiv.org L26:   * 2025.06.01 Co-authored paper is out. The title is \"Effects of Color Discrimination of Perceived Objects by Cognitive Speech Acts on the Reaction Time.\" The paper is cite9†here†doi.org .\nL27:   * 2025.05.29 Oral presentation at the 39th Annual Conference of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Analysis of the El Farol Bar Problem by LLM Agents.\"\nL28:   * 2025.04.01 Appointed as a JSPS Research Fellow PD and Project Researcher at the Graduate School of Engineering, The University of Tokyo.\nL29:   * 2025.03.24 Completed graduate school at the University of Tokyo and received a Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) degree.\nL30:   * 2025.03.01 Article published in the Journal of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"JSAI Meets AI Standardization -- Panel Discussion Report: What Personnel Are Required for the Standardization Process? --\"\nL31: ## 2024 (13)\nL32:   * 2024.12.13 Paper is out. The title is \"Spontaneous Emergence of Agent Individuality Through Social Interactions in Large Language Model-Based Communities.\" The paper is cite10†here†doi.org .\nL33:   * 2024.12.05 The article about JSAI2024 award is posted on the website of the Graduate School of Arts and Sciences, The University of Tokyo. The article is cite11†here†www.c.u-tokyo.ac.jp .\nL34:   * 2024.12.03 Preprint published. The title is \"Evolution of Collective AI Beyond Individual Optimization.\" cite12†arXiv:2412.02085†arxiv.org L35:   * 2024.11.05 Preprint published. The title is \"Spontaneous Emergence of Agent Individuality through Social Interactions in LLM-Based Communities.\" cite13†arXiv:2411.03252†arxiv.org L36:   * 2024.11.01 Article published in the Journal of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Students Forum (125) Interview with Prof. Kiyoshi Izumi -- From Complex Systems to Causal AI: Future of Financial Informatics.\"\nL37:   * 2024.10.14 Poster presentation at the 41st Annual Meeting of Japanese Cognitive Science Society (JCSS2024). The title is \"Personality Differentiation through Collective Interaction of LLM Agents.\"\nL38:   * 2024.09.01 Article published in the Journal of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Students Forum (124) Interview with Prof. Yugo Takeuchi -- HAI in the Era of Intelligent Mass Production.\"\nL39:   * 2024.05.30 Oral presentation at the 38th Annual Conference of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Emergence of New Strategies for Gaming through Collective Interaction of LLM Agents.\" And received the JSAI Annual Conference Student Incentive Award.\nL40:   * 2024.05.12 Article published in the Journal of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Students Forum (122) Interview with Roy Sugimura -- The Frontiers of AI International Standardization as Seen by Going Outside.\"\nL41:   * 2024.04.10 Lecture at the University of Tokyo VR Center Metaverse Seminar. The title is \"Simulation of LLM Agents Emanating Individuality from Collectivity in Virtual Reality.\"\nL42:   * 2024.03.25 Introduced the student session of JSAI2024. The video is cite14†here†youtu.be .\nL43:   * 2024.03.07 Received the FOST Award for my research results, which were funded by the foudation for the Fusion Of Science and Technology (FOST) as Principal Investigator.\nL44:   * 2024.03.05 Oral presentation at the HAI Symposium 2024. The title is \"Interaction of LLM Agents Emerging Individuality from Collectivity.\" And received the Student Encouragement Award.\nL45: ## 2023 (8)\nL46:   * 2023.12.18 Lecture at the University of Tokyo VR Center Doctoral Symposium. The title is \"Evolution of Swarm and Neural Network Dynamics Based on Chemotaxis.\"\nL47:   * 2023.10.08 Presentation at the final audition of the PhD Idol Project.\nL48:   * 2023.09.19 Co-authored preprint published. The title is \"PAMS: Platform for Artificial Market Simulations.\" cite15†arXiv:2309.10729†arxiv.org L49:   * 2023.09.07-2023.09.09 Poster presentation at the 40th Annual Meeting of the Japanese Cognitive Science Society. The title is \"Cognitive Modeling of Thrill-Seeking Irrational Behavior with Conflicting Adaptive Optimizations.\"\nL50:   * 2023.07.23-2023.07.28 Poster presentation at ALIFE2023. The title is \"Evolving Collective AI: Simulation of Ants Communicating via Chemicals.\"\nL51:   * 2023.06.08 Organized the student session \"What do people want from Artificial Intelligence\" at JSAI2023.\nL52:   * 2023.03.05 Poster presentation at the HAI Symposium 2023. The title is \"A Cognitive Model of Thrill Using Evolutionary Computation and Reinforcement Learning.\"\nL53:   * 2023.02.17-2023.02.19 Developed the VR system for the VR installation work cite16†\"Mind Time Machine II\"†mtm2.alternativemachine.co.jp .\nL54: ## 2022 (7)\nL55:   * 2022.11.23 Oral presentation at the ALife Japan Workshop #5. The title is \"Emergence of Collective Behavior through Evolution of Individuals and Interaction.\"\nL56:   * 2022.09.05 Received Ikeda Scientific Co. Bridge Fellowship Grants. The research theme is \"Modeling Group Emergence Based on Learning in Play.\"\nL57:   * 2022.08.25 Received GCP (Google Cloud Platform) Credit Award and $12,000 GCP Credits. The research theme is \"Artificial Life Study in Simulated Environments.\"\nL58:   * 2022.07.01 Poster presentation at the ALife Japan Workshop #4. The title is \"Emergence of Organized Behavior through Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning of Kick the Can Game.\"\nL59:   * 2022.03.17 Received master degree at the Shizuoka University Degree Conferral Ceremony, representing 378 students in the master's program. Also received the Dean's Award of Informatics, for outstanding academic achievement. The article is cite17†here†www.inf.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL60:   * 2022.03.04-2022.03.05 Poster presentation at the Hyper Interdisciplinary Conference 2022. The title is \"Development of a Cognitive Model of Thrill-Seeking.\" And he received the Career Design Research Center Award.\nL61:   * 2022.03.02-2022.03.03 Oral presentation at the HAI Symposium 2022. The title is \"Analysis of Group Organization and Dynamics through Reinforcement Learning in \"Kick the Can\" Game.\"\nL62: ## 2021 (6)\nL63:   * 2021.12.23 Received an Outstanding Achievement Award at Shizuoka University and was exempted from paying tuition for the second semester. The article is cite18†here†www.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL64:   * 2021.12.17 Accepted for a research grant from the foudation for the Fusion Of Science and Technology (FOST). The research theme is \"Developing NPCs that Thrill by Combining Instinct and Learned Value Functions.\" The result is cite19†here†www.fost.or.jp .\nL65:   * 2021.09.03-2021.09.05 Oral presentation (online) at the 38th Annual Meeting of the Japanese Cognitive Science Society. The title is \"Reinforcement Learning Agents Solving the Mutual Prediction Problem through Different Standpoints.\"\nL66:   * 2021.06.08-2021.06.11 Oral presentation (online) at the 35th Annual Conference of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Acquiring Cooperative Behavior through Reinforcement Learning of Winning Strategy.\"\nL67:   * 2021.03.17-2021.05.28 In the toio Do! contest, my work passed the first screening (idea solicitation), the second screening (work submission), and won the Special Jury Award at the final judging session. The award-winning work is cite20†here†protopedia.net . And cite21†here†www.youtube.com is the judging process.\nL68:   * 2021.03.09-2021.03.10 Oral presentation (online) at the HAI Symposium 2021. The title is \"Cooperation without Person Perception on Kick the Can Game.\" And received the Student Encouragement Award.\nL69: ## 2020 (7)\nL70:   * 2020.12.03 Won the Special Jury Award for my YouTube video in the \"Let's Do Robots! toio & Unity Movie Contest.\" The winning video is cite22†here†youtu.be .\nL71:   * 2020.11.07 Participated in the 3rd Shizuoka Tech Plan Grand Prix with the HAI-NE team. Our title is \"Interpersonal communication support based on HAI design methodology.\" And our team won the Grand Prize (300,000 yen), the Yamaha Motor Prize (100,000 yen), and the Hamamatsu Iwata Shinkin Bank Prize (100,000 yen). The article is cite23†here†www.inf.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL72:   * 2020.10.17-2020.10.18 Oral presentation (online) at Human Interface Cyber Colloquium. The title is \"Group Formation and Behavioral Analysis of Kick the Can by Agents Using Reinforcement Learning.\" Received the Best Presentation Award.\nL73:   * 2020.09.17-2020.09.19 Poster presentation (online) at the 37th Annual Meeting of the Japanese Cognitive Science Society. The title is \"Physical Interaction of Kick the Can Using Reinforcement Learning.\"\nL74:   * 2020.06.09-2020.06.12 Poster presentation (online) at the 34th Annual Conference of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence. The title is \"Analysis of Cooperative Interaction between Creatures Using Neuroevolution.\"\nL75:   * 2020.03.06-2020.03.07 Oral presentation (online) at the HAI Symposium 2020. The title is \"Automatic Acquisition of Cooperative Behavior by Creatures through Reinforcement Learning.\"\nL76:   * 2020.02.29-2020.03.01 Oral presentation (online) as a finalist at the 9th Science Intercollegiate Meeting. The title is \"Analysis of Coevolution and Motivation in Action Game AI: A Case Study of Bomberman.\"\nL77: ## 2019 (4)\nL78:   * 2019.12.12 Received an Outstanding Achievement Award at Shizuoka University and was exempted from paying tuition for the second semester. The article is cite24†here†www.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL79:   * 2019.10.06-2019.10.10 Oral and poster presentations at the international conference HAI2019. The title is \"Design of Cooperative Interaction between Humans and AI Creatures through Reinforcement Learning.\"\nL80:   * 2019.08.21 Participated in Hack U 2019 NAGOYA, a student hackathon organized by Yahoo! JAPAN.\nL81:   * 2019.03.02-2019.03.03 Oral presentation as a finalist at the 8th Science Intercollegiate. The title is \"Self Learning Method for Discovering the Secret Tricks of Action Games: A Case Study of Super Mario Bros.\" And received the Special Jury Award (50,000 yen). The article is cite25†here†www.inf.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL82: ## 2018 (4)\nL83:   * 2018.12.15 Participated in the \"Regional Development in Shizuoka - Realization of Regional Development through Apps\" Hackathon. Won the Special Jury Award. The article is cite26†here†www.inf.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL84:   * 2018.09.29 Participated in the \"Regional Development in Shizuoka - Realization of Regional Development through Apps\" ideathon. Won the Unique Idea Award. The article is cite27†here†www.inf.shizuoka.ac.jp .\nL85:   * 2018.03.16 At the graduation ceremony of National Institute of Technology, Matsue College, he recieved The Institute of Electrical and Information Engineers Award, the Distinguished Service Award, the Outstanding Achievement Award, and the Outstanding Graduate Student Award.\nL86:   * 2018.03.02-2018.03.03 Oral presentation at the 39th Annual Conference on Game Informatics. The title is \"Proposal of A Self Learning Method to Discover Secret Tricks Using Infinite 1-up as The Theme.\" And he eceived the Young Scientist Encouragement Award. The article is cite28†here†www.matsue-ct.jp .\nL87: ## 2017 (2)\nL88: \nL89:   * 2017.03.25 Talked with Matz and Ayaka Ikezawa at the talk session of the 2nd Smalruby Programming Koshien.\nL90:   * 2017.01.06-2017.01.08 Poster presentation at the 58th Programming Symposium. The title is \"Introduction of Making AI Program for the 1st 'Smalruby Koshien' and its Future Prospects.\"\nL91: ## 2016 (10)\nL92:   * 2016.11.26-2016.11.27 Participated in \"Challenge with RESAS-API! Hackathon for Regional Development in Shimane\".\nL93:   * 2016.09.24 Individual and group exhibits at the student zone exhibition booth at Open Source Conference 2016 Shimane.\nL94:   * 2016.09.17 Lectured at the Smalruby Programming Koshien Experience Seminar held at Matsue Open Source Lab.\nL95:   * 2016.09.10-2016.09.11 Participated in the Hiyaoroshi GO hackathon held at the old house \"Fujinbo\".\nL96:   * 2016.08.29-2016.09.09 Participated in an internship at the Network Applied Communication Laboratory.\nL97:   * 2016.08.21 Won 1st place in the 100m breaststroke and 1st place in the 200m breaststroke at the 51st National Institute of Technology Championships. Also received a special commendation from the National College of Technology Athletic Meet for winning the 100m breaststroke for three consecutive years.\nL98:   * 2016.03.26 Participated in the finals of the first Smalruby Programming Koshien and won. The article is cite29†here†www.matsue-ct.jp .\nL99:   * 2016.02.29-2016.03.04 Participated in a Ruby camp and developed and presented a game using Arduino.\nL100:   * 2016.02.21 Participated in the 164th Western Honshu Indoor Swimming Competition. Won the Outstanding Athlete Award at the last swimming competition in high school.\nL101:   * 2016.01.11 Received the Outstanding Athlete Award at a ceremony in Matsue City.\nL102: ## 2015 (2)\nL103: \nL104:   * 2015.08.30 Won 1st place in 100m breaststroke and 1st place in 200m breaststroke at the 50th National Institute of Technology Championships.\nL105:   * 2015.07.12 Won the prefectural championships (1st place in the prefecture) in the 100m breaststroke and 200m breaststroke at the Shimane Prefectural Swimming Championships. The article is cite30†here†shimane-suiren.jp .\nL106: ## 2014 (2)\nL107: \nL108:   * 2014.08.24 Won 1st place in 100m breaststroke, 2nd place in 200m breaststroke at the 49th National Institute of Technology Championships.\nL109:   * 2014.07.13 Won the prefectural championship (1st place in the prefecture) in the 100m breaststroke at the Shimane Prefectural Swimming Championships. The article is cite31†here†shimane-suiren.jp .\nL110: ## 2012 (1)\nL111: \nL112:   * 2012.11.28 Oral presentation as a representative of a junior high school in the Shimane Research and Study Presentation Contest, and won the Excellence Award.\nL113: \nL114: ## 2011 (1)\nL115: \nL116:   * 2011.09.02 Oral presentation as a representative of a junior high school at the 2011 Juvenile Claims Matsue Convention, and won the Excellence Award.\nL117: \nL118: (c) Ryosuke Takata. Powered by cite32†Jekyll†jekyllrb.com . Updated at 11 Sep 2026.\n"
